578
00:20:15,848 --> 00:20:17,207
What's this?

579
00:20:17,208 --> 00:20:18,218
(A very unfamiliar pork cutlet)

580
00:20:18,448 --> 00:20:20,748
I want to hear the explanation before trying this one. Sir?

581
00:20:21,288 --> 00:20:23,117
Let me explain.

582
00:20:23,118 --> 00:20:26,087
I combined three types of Japanese curry to make this.

583
00:20:26,088 --> 00:20:29,857
I used corn as an ingredient.

584
00:20:29,858 --> 00:20:30,858
(Corn-flavoured curry)

585
00:20:30,859 --> 00:20:32,998
The black thing is menchi katsu.

586
00:20:33,258 --> 00:20:36,667
It's made with ground beef, ground pork,

587
00:20:36,668 --> 00:20:38,438
and onions.

588
00:20:38,838 --> 00:20:41,638
I season it with a special soy sauce...

589
00:20:42,108 --> 00:20:45,637
and coat it in squid ink breadcrumbs to give it a unique appearance.

590
00:20:45,638 --> 00:20:48,108
(Coated in squid ink breadcrumbs for a more unusual look)

591
00:20:50,008 --> 00:20:52,878
Break it up with a spoon, mix everything, and enjoy.

592
00:20:53,978 --> 00:20:55,417
Let me try this.

593
00:20:55,418 --> 00:20:56,687
It breaks apart easily.

594
00:20:56,688 --> 00:20:59,257
- It's made with ground meat, - Right.

595
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:01,457
so it's easy to cut. The attention to detail...

596
00:21:01,458 --> 00:21:02,458
(Impressed by the details)

597
00:21:02,988 --> 00:21:06,257
Even elderly people with dental problems could enjoy this.

598
00:21:06,258 --> 00:21:07,698
(Easy to cut and pop straight into your mouth)

599
00:21:11,168 --> 00:21:13,137
(Exclaiming)

600
00:21:13,138 --> 00:21:15,438
The curry is incredibly savoury.

601
00:21:15,908 --> 00:21:17,007
The curry is so good.

602
00:21:17,008 --> 00:21:18,008
(A round of applause)

603
00:21:18,009 --> 00:21:19,108
He clapped.

604
00:21:19,708 --> 00:21:21,978
- Try it. - It's not every day...

605
00:21:22,248 --> 00:21:24,278
- you see Jae Seok clapping. - It's rare.

606
00:21:25,748 --> 00:21:27,688
(Clapping)

607
00:21:27,918 --> 00:21:29,288
- Sir. - Yes?

608
00:21:31,288 --> 00:21:33,188
- Are you tired? - No.

609
00:21:33,758 --> 00:21:36,257
(His voice sounds quite exhausted.)

610
00:21:36,258 --> 00:21:38,327
Is this 32 dollars per person?

611
00:21:38,328 --> 00:21:40,498
- It's 38 dollars. - It's 38 dollars?

612
00:21:40,898 --> 00:21:43,227
- Aren't you charging too little? - That means something.

613
00:21:43,228 --> 00:21:45,197
- It's too cheap. - This is...

614
00:21:45,198 --> 00:21:47,268
Are we in Songpa?

615
00:21:47,638 --> 00:21:50,438
It's not like the land here is incredibly cheap here.

616
00:21:50,468 --> 00:21:53,577
- Considering the location... - Exactly.

617
00:21:53,578 --> 00:21:54,677
(Considering the location and quality, the price is low.)

618
00:21:54,678 --> 00:21:56,477
This might be very nosy,

619
00:21:56,478 --> 00:21:58,017
but the regular customers who come here might think,

620
00:21:58,018 --> 00:21:59,718
"What are they talking about?"

621
00:22:01,748 --> 00:22:03,588
"They showed up out of nowhere..."

622
00:22:03,948 --> 00:22:05,588
"and are talking nonsense."

623
00:22:06,188 --> 00:22:07,558
They could be thinking that.

624
00:22:07,728 --> 00:22:09,227
- That's possible. - Right?

625
00:22:09,228 --> 00:22:10,457
Of course, you're right.

626
00:22:10,458 --> 00:22:12,397
But from our perspective,

627
00:22:12,398 --> 00:22:13,958
this is quite valuable.

628
00:22:14,668 --> 00:22:16,497
(I agree.)

629
00:22:16,498 --> 00:22:18,337
- Here's your next dish. - Okay.

630
00:22:18,338 --> 00:22:21,108
This is tsukemen. You should dip the noodles into the broth.

631
00:22:21,738 --> 00:22:24,538
Gosh, I love tsukemen.

632
00:22:24,838 --> 00:22:27,377
It's served with shoyu ramen.

633
00:22:27,378 --> 00:22:28,977
(Lastly, it's tsukemen and shoyu ramen.)

634
00:22:28,978 --> 00:22:31,978
I make the noodles myself.

635
00:22:32,118 --> 00:22:34,047
The sauce and broth are made by simmering Korean chicken...

636
00:22:34,048 --> 00:22:36,018
for six hours.

637
00:22:36,488 --> 00:22:39,357
You can either dip the noodles or enjoy them in the broth.

638
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:41,018
I serve two different types.

639
00:22:42,058 --> 00:22:45,598
(A refreshing finish that settles your heavy stomach)

640
00:22:46,658 --> 00:22:50,198
(Slurping in)

641
00:22:50,398 --> 00:22:52,038
It cuts through the greasiness.

642
00:22:54,938 --> 00:23:01,548
(A light noodle dish to wrap up the pork cutlet course)

643
00:23:01,578 --> 00:23:03,307
(Humming)

644
00:23:03,308 --> 00:23:04,578
Tsukemen.

645
00:23:05,648 --> 00:23:06,748
(Exclaiming)

646
00:23:07,788 --> 00:23:08,817
(Glancing)

647
00:23:08,818 --> 00:23:10,747
BIBI is really enjoying herself...

648
00:23:10,748 --> 00:23:13,087
ever since Waterbomb.

649
00:23:13,088 --> 00:23:14,928
(Job satisfaction at its peak)

650
00:23:15,358 --> 00:23:17,057
(Diet restrictions are lifted.)

651
00:23:17,058 --> 00:23:18,058
This is incredible.

652
00:23:18,059 --> 00:23:19,227
(This is incredible.)

653
00:23:19,228 --> 00:23:20,298
That's so cute.

654
00:23:21,428 --> 00:23:22,498
Are you also...

655
00:23:23,398 --> 00:23:25,198
- from Gyeongsang Province? - Gyeongsang...

656
00:23:26,198 --> 00:23:28,467
- My senior. - I'm so happy to hear that.

657
00:23:28,468 --> 00:23:29,907
- Me too. Nice to meet you. - Nice to meet you too.

658
00:23:29,908 --> 00:23:31,007
Where are you from?

659
00:23:31,008 --> 00:23:32,377
I'm from Jinhae.

660
00:23:32,378 --> 00:23:33,508
- You're from Jinhae. - Jinhae?

661
00:23:33,538 --> 00:23:35,747
I'm from Changwon.

662
00:23:35,748 --> 00:23:36,748
- By the way... - That's a big city.

663
00:23:36,749 --> 00:23:38,848
Both Jin Young and I are from the same hometown.

664
00:23:38,978 --> 00:23:39,978
Are you also from Jinhae?

665
00:23:39,979 --> 00:23:41,147
- From Jinhae? - I'm from Jinhae.

666
00:23:41,148 --> 00:23:42,247
(Jin Young is also a man of Jinhae.)

667
00:23:42,248 --> 00:23:44,017
I used to be afraid of Jinhae.

668
00:23:44,018 --> 00:23:46,818
I was scared of guys riding motorcycles in Jinhae.

669
00:23:47,318 --> 00:23:48,428
I wasn't one of them.

670
00:23:48,628 --> 00:23:50,627
People in Jinhae were scared of those in Changwon and Masan.

671
00:23:50,628 --> 00:23:51,657
- Really? - Yes.

672
00:23:51,658 --> 00:23:53,598
- You were wary of each other. - Right.

673
00:23:53,928 --> 00:23:56,367
- We were scared of each other. - You were scared of each other.

674
00:23:56,368 --> 00:23:58,567
I'm sorry, but is this "Midnight Diner?"

675
00:23:58,568 --> 00:24:01,067
(I'm sorry, but is this "Midnight Diner?")

676
00:24:01,068 --> 00:24:02,307
The vibe became...

677
00:24:02,308 --> 00:24:04,678
- It's the vibe of "Midnight Diner." - Right.

678
00:24:05,308 --> 00:24:08,277
We should check out other places first, don't you think?

679
00:24:08,278 --> 00:24:09,507
- Yes. - Right?

680
00:24:09,508 --> 00:24:10,948
(Pork cutlet omakase, 1. An undeniably perfect taste...)

681
00:24:11,218 --> 00:24:12,448
Today's theme is...

682
00:24:12,648 --> 00:24:14,788
- You Seem Unfamiliar Today. - Unfamiliar Today.

683
00:24:14,888 --> 00:24:16,718
I kept talking about this earlier.

684
00:24:16,918 --> 00:24:18,557
It's a place where Korean customers come,

685
00:24:18,558 --> 00:24:21,258
but there were Japanese magazines...

686
00:24:21,428 --> 00:24:25,757
and records. Of course, they're related to Japan.

687
00:24:25,758 --> 00:24:27,197
(The interior was designed to fit the concept, but...)

688
00:24:27,198 --> 00:24:30,268
It all felt unfamiliar to me.

689
00:24:30,698 --> 00:24:31,897
(Thinking)

690
00:24:31,898 --> 00:24:33,168
There was nothing special about it.

691
00:24:34,038 --> 00:24:36,008
Sun Kyu, isn't it just unfamiliar to you?

692
00:24:37,208 --> 00:24:38,337
I guess so.

693
00:24:38,338 --> 00:24:40,238
The intercessory prayer is working on you.

694
00:24:40,708 --> 00:24:42,748
Here's what's impressive about Sun Kyu.

695
00:24:42,948 --> 00:24:44,917
He's very funny, but when the shoot starts...

696
00:24:44,918 --> 00:24:47,518
- Isn't he different? - He's not funny at all.

697
00:24:48,188 --> 00:24:49,988
So it was hard to work with Sun Kyu.

698
00:24:50,248 --> 00:24:51,887
- In what way? - I kept laughing,

699
00:24:51,888 --> 00:24:54,357
but Sun Kyu was the only one who was serious.

700
00:24:54,358 --> 00:24:55,528
(Sun Kyu switched straight into villain mode.)

701
00:24:55,728 --> 00:24:56,887
Isn't it the same director...

702
00:24:56,888 --> 00:24:58,598
- as "Extraordinary Attorney Woo?" - That's right.

703
00:24:59,098 --> 00:25:00,698
- Is it Director Yoo In Sik? - Director Yoo In Sik.

704
00:25:01,368 --> 00:25:03,298
He's the director of "Extraordinary Attorney Woo."

705
00:25:04,228 --> 00:25:06,037
I'd like to work with him.

706
00:25:06,038 --> 00:25:07,068
You?

707
00:25:07,368 --> 00:25:08,737
(Work on what?)

708
00:25:08,738 --> 00:25:09,767
I can still dream, can't I?

709
00:25:09,768 --> 00:25:12,037
Ask him to appear on Sixth Sense.

710
00:25:12,038 --> 00:25:13,038
Why not?

711
00:25:13,039 --> 00:25:14,337
He's very cheerful...

712
00:25:14,338 --> 00:25:15,577
- He's funny. - and funny.

713
00:25:15,578 --> 00:25:17,178
- Right? - I thought so too.

714
00:25:17,508 --> 00:25:21,518
I really enjoyed Jin Young's drama before his last one.

715
00:25:21,748 --> 00:25:23,147
- "Our Unwritten Seoul?" - Yes.

716
00:25:23,148 --> 00:25:24,188
Thank you.

717
00:25:24,688 --> 00:25:29,628
(Jin Young played Lee So Hoo, the sweetest boyfriend ever.)

718
00:25:30,258 --> 00:25:31,957
(His tender performance made him the ultimate boyfriend material,)

719
00:25:31,958 --> 00:25:33,858
(leaving viewers dreaming of marriage.)

720
00:25:34,498 --> 00:25:35,627
Seriously.

721
00:25:35,628 --> 00:25:37,198
(Nostalgic)

722
00:25:37,228 --> 00:25:38,337
- Gosh. - But guys...

723
00:25:38,338 --> 00:25:41,608
that handsome and sweet don't exist in real life.

724
00:25:42,308 --> 00:25:44,837
Like the character in the drama.

725
00:25:44,838 --> 00:25:47,077
- That's so sad. - They don't exist in real life.

726
00:25:47,078 --> 00:25:48,407
There's Jae Seok.

727
00:25:48,408 --> 00:25:51,007
- Jae Seok is sweet, - Right.

728
00:25:51,008 --> 00:25:53,018
but he doesn't look handsome like Jin Young.

729
00:25:53,818 --> 00:25:55,117
You don't know this,

730
00:25:55,118 --> 00:25:58,018
but CEO Song cares a lot about looks.

731
00:25:58,088 --> 00:25:59,387
I really do.

732
00:25:59,388 --> 00:26:03,228
Her standards are as high as the sky.

733
00:26:04,288 --> 00:26:06,758
I didn't see anything suspicious about the first place.

734
00:26:07,228 --> 00:26:10,097
If I had to be suspicious, I can find things to question.

735
00:26:10,098 --> 00:26:11,228
Maybe the awkward atmosphere?

736
00:26:11,468 --> 00:26:13,038
I thought that it was fake.

737
00:26:13,268 --> 00:26:15,607
- Why? - They tried to bring...

738
00:26:15,608 --> 00:26:17,467
- everything under one vibe. - Was it strange?

739
00:26:17,468 --> 00:26:19,608
- Okay. - But something felt off.

740
00:26:20,338 --> 00:26:21,407
(Is this place fake?)

741
00:26:21,408 --> 00:26:23,308
(Japanese items that the production crew gathered in a hurry?)

742
00:26:23,508 --> 00:26:27,878
I really hope that it's real.

743
00:26:28,118 --> 00:26:29,718
- To go back there after the shoot? - Yes.

744
00:26:30,718 --> 00:26:32,388
I would absolutely love it.

745
00:26:33,888 --> 00:26:35,557
The fried food was so good.

746
00:26:35,558 --> 00:26:36,687
- Right. - I agree.

747
00:26:36,688 --> 00:26:39,098
- It's hard to believe it's fake. - Right.

748
00:26:39,428 --> 00:26:42,698
Two minutes ago, Jin Young said that it was fake.

749
00:26:43,698 --> 00:26:44,797
But just now...

750
00:26:44,798 --> 00:26:46,467
You keep changing your mind, Jin Young.

751
00:26:46,468 --> 00:26:47,898
(You keep changing your mind.)

752
00:26:47,968 --> 00:26:49,368
My heart sways like a reed.

753
00:26:50,168 --> 00:26:52,108
You gave it the highest praise when we were eating.

754
00:26:52,208 --> 00:26:53,208
That's true.

755
00:26:53,209 --> 00:26:54,877
After giving it the highest praise, as soon as you came out...

756
00:26:54,878 --> 00:26:57,308
(I thought that it was fake.)

757
00:26:57,948 --> 00:27:00,578
(The most handsome reed in the world)

758
00:27:00,948 --> 00:27:02,087
We're going quite far.

759
00:27:02,088 --> 00:27:04,148
We crossed the bridge and made it over to Gangnam.

760
00:27:08,458 --> 00:27:09,487
(They get out of the car first.)

761
00:27:09,488 --> 00:27:11,458
- Thank you. - Thank you.

762
00:27:12,658 --> 00:27:14,967
(Located on a peaceful alley, a building with a neat exterior)

763
00:27:14,968 --> 00:27:16,668
This place has a totally different vibe.

764
00:27:17,268 --> 00:27:18,938
- What? - This is...

765
00:27:20,598 --> 00:27:21,707
A restaurant?

766
00:27:21,708 --> 00:27:22,808
(Is this the restaurant?)

767
00:27:25,208 --> 00:27:27,077
(It helps regulate your blood sugar naturally.)

768
00:27:27,078 --> 00:27:29,407
(Thank you, chef.)

769
00:27:29,408 --> 00:27:30,648
(Second location: On-site reaction hint)

770
00:27:31,008 --> 00:27:34,687
